Z||000000||ounmongk||07-15-2000||02:23 AM||||hey hey! I've bought a Bazooka tube from a local pawn shop for $50, came with a replacement sub in it though, I guess the stock one was blown? When I hooked it up to a reciever/amplifier my dad had,BY GEORGE, it shook the house!!! it's only an 8" too! in any case, I need to hook up an amp in the car... any tips on this? anything I should know? or is it a plain-jane simple installation? Thanks, everyone. <BR>Ohm. ||||reg||7
Z||000001||olympic||07-15-2000||03:38 AM||||  Use at least 8 guage wire for + and - power.  Run the + directly to the battery with an inline fuse near the battery.  The - wire should be as short as possible and grounded to bare chassis metal.  Keep the rca patch cord away from other wires. Dont ground the chassis of the amp.  Mount it to wood or plastic.  Nothing should cover the cooling fins on the amp.  It should have atleast 2" of space for air circulation.  Also, dont crank the gain on the amp to maximum.  To set the gain properly, turn the volume on your deck up to about 80% and then slowly turn the gain up on the amp until you can hear the sub start to distort then back it off a little.  oh, yeah, and dont forget to have fun!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>"Born free....taxed to death."||||reg||1
Z||000002||KevinP||07-15-2000||01:08 PM||||One more bit of info.  When running your positive power line, You will quickly dicover that there really isn't any good places in the firewall to run a wire through (existing or otherwise).  I ran it along the rockerpanel and up along the wheel well and made a small cut by the battery.  Also, when tuning the amp, set the low-pass filter level a little high.  Since you are running an 8", you will be able to get some good punch in your mids.<BR>Latta'<P>Kevin||||reg||3
Z||000003||ounmongk||07-15-2000||01:37 PM||||cool, thanks again. one more thing, though: anyone with Bazooka tubes, how did you mount the tube in your car? I think Loki had a 10" tube in his car, but I forget how it was put in... Velco tape? maybe I can just put it on the passenger seat vertically and paste little eyes and ears on it to make it look like a real person!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Seriously, though... the tube is made of wood, would anyone recommend screws to fasten the tube to the car? <BR>Ohm <p>[This message has been edited by ounmongk (edited 07-15-2000).]||||reg||1
